    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d351-a11">

                <pb facs="0487" n="381" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg381"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 8.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Consul-General Rodgers to Minister
                    Rockhill.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Consular Service</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-07-27"><hi rendition="#italic">July 27,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your No. 97, concerning the road to the hills and the altering of the rules
                    of the mixed court at Shanghai.</p>
                <p>In reply I beg to inform you that both of these subjects were discussed at a
                    meeting of the consular body Wednesday, the conclusion being to do nothing. No
                    report has been received from the viceroy on the question of the road. As to the
                    mixed court, I shall instruct our assessor to adhere to the established rules
                    until changes are authorized from Peking.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>(Signed) <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James L.
                    Rodgers.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
